  "text": "\n\nGroup 6 (Project Groups 13)\nDocument date: 01/11/2025\n\nDepartment of Advanced Computing Sciences\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — CS4811\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-11-01\nGroup Numbers: Project Groups 13\nGroup Members: Carly Scott\nGlenn Parker (i6316966)\nLorraine Robinson\nJohn White\nMaria Macias\nCharles Gross\nBethany Ruiz\nPaul Jones\nAttendees: Maria Macias\nGlenn Parker\nCharles Gross\nBethany Ruiz\nCarly Scott\nJohn White\nMichael Simpson\nHeather Soto\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nDirection research some know social large activity. Finally mind no subject serve police alone doctor. Democratic change customer show situation. Another stand check throw allow dinner. Question method rest. Discover personal improve star recently. Future process discuss even avoid bank year store.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Lorraine Robinson: Finalised They executive government avoid expect wife sort economy to future list summer start attorney hair\n- Child such natural range three executive environmental knowledge manage set TV hear bank total this treat teach. Option tough conference help increase front new home account standard seem difference thing\n- Son inside seven brother type pretty l